From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tzarial <zork@google.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:41:46 +0000
Subject: GL: Fix UAF in ContextGL with depth init PBOs

ContextGL declared mDepthInitPBOs before mRenderer in the class
definition, causing mRenderer to be destroyed before mDepthInitPBOs
during ~ContextGL(). If mRenderer was the last shared_ptr, RendererGL
and its FunctionsGL were freed before ~PixelBufferGL() attempted to
call functions->deleteBuffers(), resulting in a heap-use-after-free.

This CL fixes the issue by:
1. Moving mRenderer before mDepthInitPBOs so member destruction order
   guarantees mDepthInitPBOs is destroyed while mRenderer is still
   valid.
2. Implementing ContextGL::onDestroy to clear mDepthInitPBOs on
   context destruction.

Bug: b/550379413
Test: EGLContextASANTest.DestroyContextWithRobustDepthInitPBO/*
Change-Id: Iefab278ad75b7ef6a45a64db7dbd6876498bdff0
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8308574
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Tzarial <zork@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
ContextGL.h: context drift only (the branch declares
applyRecreateFboWorkaroundIfNeeded next to the moved members); the
protected/private reordering is applied verbatim.

